\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thou Shepherd of Israel, and mine,
\par The joy and desire of my heart,
\par For closer communion I pine,
\par I long to reside where Thou art:
\par The pasture I languish to find
\par Where all, who their Shepherd obey,
\par Are fed, on Thy bosom reclined,
\par And sreened from the heat of the day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Ah! show me that happiest place,
\par The place of Thy people's abode,
\par Where saints in an ecstasy gaze,
\par And hang on a crucified God;
\par Thy love for a sinner declare,
\par Thy passion  and death on the tree;
\par My spirit to Calvary bear,
\par To suffer and triumph with Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. 'Tis there, with the lambs of Thy flock,
\par There only, I covet to rest,
\par To lie at the foot of the rock,
\par Or rise to be hid in Thy breast;
\par 'Tis there I would  always abide,
\par And never a moment depart,
\par Concealed in the cleft of Thy side,
\par Eternally held in Thy heart.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
